I built you something — since the workspace was empty and you said "do something you want," I made a small, polished, fully-offline **Pomodoro focus timer with a stats dashboard**: `/workspace/focus.html`.

**What it does**
- **Focus / short-break / long-break** timer with a circular progress ring, phase tabs, start/pause/reset, and a beep on completion. Every 4th focus round auto-flows to a long break.
- **Task list** — pick the task you're working on; each completed focus round (or a manual `+25` button) logs minutes toward it. Editable, deletable, color-coded.
- **KPIs** — focus today, rounds today, day streak, and best day (last 30 days).
- **Two charts** (per the dataviz skill I pulled in — validated palette, tooltips, legends, table-view twins, dark mode):
  - *Focus over time*: a sequential-blue bar chart of minutes per day, with a 7/14/30-day range selector.
  - *Where your time went*: a horizontal task-breakdown bar in the categorical palette.

Everything is **one dependency-free HTML file**, data stays in `localStorage`, nothing is sent anywhere. It seeds itself with ~30 days of sample data on first open so the charts look alive — clear `localStorage` if you want a blank slate.

**One honest caveat:** I couldn't do a final visual render. No headless browser was available and the sandbox has no network to install system libraries, so I can't confirm pixel-level layout. I did syntax-check all the JavaScript and hand-reviewed the render logic (fixed a tooltip-positioning bug, a missing `<svg>` wrapper, a local-vs-UTC date bug, and the long-break cycle along the way).

**To view it:** open it in any browser — `open /workspace/focus.html` on macOS, or drag it into a browser window.

